  "id": "COMPOUND:24672 - PROTEIN:6285",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Isoitalicene is implicated in targeting Prohibitin, which in turn acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Lycorenan-7-one,9,10-dimethoxy-1-methyl and 3,8-Dihydroxy-9-methoxypterocarpan. All three of these molecules share a common pathway where they ultimately target Macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II. This suggests a potential mechanism by which (+)-Isoitalicene may exert its effects, possibly through a similar molecular interaction that leads to the activation or modulation of these receptors. The evidence points to a convergent pathway where Prohibitin serves as a central node, with multiple downstream targets that ultimately influence macrophage function. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Prohibitin in mediating the effects of various compounds, including (+)-Isoitalicene, and underscores the role of scavenger receptors in the cellular response to these molecules.",
